hey quick announcement the channel now  has official merge head on to  crowdmate.com using the link in the  description or through the pin to  comment okay on with the video  [Music]  rome nicknamed the eternal city it's  well known for its museums from the  frescoed paintings of the vatican to the  abandoned ruins of the roman forum but  there's one museum i bet you haven't  heard of a museum with a very disturbing  collection  attached to a small church there's a  quiet room that houses ghostly artifacts  with messages from beyond the grave  from dark handprints seared onto wood to  phantom markings etched in prayer books  the museum's haunting exhibits are  dedicated to the souls of the dead and  record their eerie communications with  the living  it has to be one of the most disturbing  museums around but why does it exist  what's it for and how do we know that  any of these objects are indeed genuine  welcome to strange christian art this  episode the museum of lost souls  the story of how this museum came to be  is just as dark as its contents  the little museum of purgatory as it's  known can be found in the church of the  sacred heart of suffrage it's a very  unusual church the only one in rome  built in a gothic style it looks out of  place amongst the baroque domes and  renaissance arches the building you see  today is not the first church on this  site in fact the original had burnt down  in a fire it was the evening of the 15th  of september 1897 when smoke was seen  rising from the church's roof by that  point it was too late the old rafters  and beams were already ablaze  all parishioners and priests could do  was look unhelplessly as their place of  worship was consumed by fire one of the  onlookers father victor jouer is said to  have seen something very strange within  the flames looking back at him was the  face of a man he had an anguished  expression and looked to be in pain  surveying the damage the next day the  same face had been burned onto a wall a  deeply religious man the priest took  this as a sign  this face he believed was the soul of a  man trapped in purgatory a middle realm  between heaven and hell  as the church began reconstruction he  set out to travel around europe looking  for more evidence of lost souls  for those unfamiliar with the idea  purgatory is the place for those who are  not quite good enough for heaven but  also not quite evil enough for hell  purgatory is the destiny for the  mediocre for those who fell slightly  short of heaven's demanding entry  requirements to escape purgatory souls  have to purge themselves of all  remaining sin often by completing  difficult trials or having loved ones  praying on their behalf  in doing so they will be allowed to  proceed and finally enter heaven the  idea of purgatory is not universally  accepted amongst christians especially  as it's not really mentioned in the  bible the concept seems to date to the  middle ages to a legend about an 11th  century abbot called odilo of clooney in  one version of the story he'd been  shipwrecked on a mysterious island there  he met a hermit who told him about a  chasm where lost souls were able to  escape the clutches of hell when the  abbott returned home he established a  festival called all souls day to honor  the dead and to offer them prayers  another writer who wrote a lot about  purgatory was the medieval poet dante  alighieri in his sequel to inferno he  envisioned purgatory as a giant mountain  in the southern hemisphere the mountain  was made up of layers of terraces each  representing one of the seven deadly  sins  in the poem dante meets with souls on  their way to heaven and describes the  difficult trials they must face in order  to proceed  for example on the first terrace pride  souls must carry heavy boulders past  statues of saints doing so would teach  them humility  on terrace 3 wrath souls must walk  through a blanket of thick acrid smoke  symbolizing how anger can blind good  judgment  on the final terrace lust souls must  pass through an intense wall of flame to  burn away all remaining sin  finally cleansing them before they enter  heaven  it's not quite the horror of dante's  inferno  but purgatory is not quite a paradise  either  in the late middle ages the doctrine of  purgatory became very popular there were  even tickets known as indulgences where  you could buy forgiveness of sin  speeding up the journey of a deceased  relative as they made their way up the  mountain but in later centuries  purgatory fell out of favor especially  in branches of christianity like  protestantism for catholics however it  still remains a core belief  [Music]  as father jouer returned from his  travels in europe he brought with him  items that supposedly proved the  existence of purgatory he had gathered a  dozen or so of these objects each with a  unique story  placing them in a small annex of the  newly constructed church he opened his  morbid collection to the public  this item exhibit 7c is a dark handprint  that has been seared onto a wooden board  in the upper corner there's a small  cross the story goes that this is the  ghostly hand of one p panzini who on the  1st of november 1731 returned as a  spirit to make this ghoulish imprint  it was followed by two more handprints  one staining a piece of parchment and  the other on a nun's robe  the ghost of your handprints came with a  plea  pray for my soul and end my suffering in  purgatory many of the other exhibits are  books with phantom markings such as  exhibit nine a german prayer book with  five finger holes burnt in the pages the  book belonged to giorgio schips who on  the 21st of december 1838 saw a set of  spectral fingerprints char the paper in  front of him apparently it was his  brother giuseppe who had died a few  months prior he asked his brother for  forgiveness to save his soul that was  trapped between heaven and hell  one of my favorites is this object  exhibit three it's a nightcap that  belonged to a man called luigi he too  was visited by a strange apparition it  turned out to be the specter of his wife  luisa whose ghostly apparition created a  small hole in the cat  another disturbing story but i think  there's a more mundane explanation to  this one if you ask me this looks more  like the work of moths who are known to  chew through clothing making these  rather distinctive round holes just a  theory  the room is full of unique exhibits like  these a book that has three ghostly  finger marks at the base  stained clothing of unknown origin and  even a haunted banknote  each one has a legend to go with it all  following a rather similar format vision  of a deceased relative a strange mark  appears  and a request for a prayer on their  behalf  as a collection this small museum  attempts to prove the existence of  purgatory showcasing the ways in which  lost souls have attempted to communicate  with the living since father zhuai's  death in 1912 nothing new has been added  unfortunately that charred face that  inspired the museum is nowhere to be  seen  as with any strange supernatural  phenomenon there's always a question of  whether any of these items are really  genuine  whether or not you believe in an  afterlife is up to you but could these  objects be fakes  for example let's look at that handprint  again it doesn't look very natural the  proportions are a bit off what's more  handprints are not completely flat like  this and instead are made up of contours  and ridges it's likely that this  handprint was simply drawn on perhaps  using a hot iron after all you can even  see a faint outline etched into the wood  i remain skeptical about some of these  exhibits but there are others that are a  little harder to explain  like the prayer book with those finger  holes how do you create those marks  without burning the rest of the paper  and indeed some of the other hand prints  like this one seem to look a bit more  natural i'm sure there are plenty of  rational explanations here but when it's  hard to figure out paranormal activity  is always a tempting option  despite these exhibits claiming to prove  the existence of purgatory the catholic  church takes a dim view to these kinds  of objects especially as they are so  easy to forge of course there are plenty  of strange relics out there but usually  they're connected to some sort of saint  often their physical remains these items  however are not technically holy relics  as they are traces of ordinary people  despite the supernatural stories about  their origin for now little is known  about them i suspect it will always be  that way  [Music]  the museum of lost songs is not for the  faint of heart where most museums  showcase things from this world our  museum is focused on what comes after  real or not these gruesome exhibits  still have an eerie feel to them there's  something unsettling about the idea of  the dead reaching back out into the  world of the living if you're ever  visiting rome i would recommend giving  the site a visit just look out for the  out of place church along the tiber  river  this little museum with its ominous  handprints and books with scars is a  mystery and a disturbing glimpse of what  might await us in the afterlife  [Music]  hey thanks for watching i had a great  time making this and i hope you enjoyed  it as well  if you like this video and want to see  more why not subscribe a like and a  comment also go a really long way oh and  do check out the channel's merch over at  crowdmade we have beanies t-shirts and  hoodies links are in description down  below  anyway i look forward to seeing you next  time  goodbye  [Music]
 

